      "writtenOn": "2023-06-15T15:09:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Actually I agree with Pierre-Clément here.\n\nI consider DRY to be profoundly important, but sometimes naming constants is not a win - especially if the values never change, are well-known, and any typo will cause things to break fairly obviously.\n\nSo I\u0027d suggest sticking with the status quo here.",
      "parentUuid": "12b384db_f142644e",
      "revId": "05204738bfb42f08570c2bd5d07a533c4942a9a0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
